Id: dbs006w
Severity: WARN
Category: services
Check: check_databases
Fix: Set password_encryption to scram-sha-256 and re-set the passwords.
References: postgresql.conf(5)
Controls: CIS 5.2; NIST IA-5(1), SC-13; ISO 5.17, 8.24; CE User access control

Passwords are stored as md5. A stolen pg_authid falls to billions of
guesses a second on commodity hardware; scram-sha-256 has been the
default since PostgreSQL 14.
